From 9338316c10c34980ed1ef3ca842f8967f740263b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:58:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] test(post): move the probe and arc post suites out of app
 on recorded input

Slice 2 of #926. The ten app suites that only generated a toolpath in
order to post it now run in crates/post/tests: fanuc_post,
probe_dialects, probe_guard, probe_report, probe_tormach,
inverted_probe, arc_planes, inverted_equivalence, inverted_post and
vertical_arc_entry (its posting half).

- The probe cycles are recorded as .cnc streams (and as .cl paths for
  probe_guard's path law) in crates/post/tests/recorded/inputs/. App's
  recorded_post_streams writes and guards them, and checks that every
  recording there has a generator.
- vertical_arc_entry splits. Generation and verify go to
  crates/motion/tests, which also guards the three contour .cl
  recordings; the posting half reads them in post.
- inverted_support and macro_b move with their suites. App's
  inverted_axis_display reads the fixture stream from its recording,
  which inverted_post guards.
- The ArcDto test stays in app (float_roundtrip). The goldens stay in
  crates/app/tests/golden.
- The xtask asset/gate-map unit tests read every crate's suites step.
  PROCESS_VERSION 32.

No new crate edge. No golden changed.

Fixes #926

